\section*{Finite étale covers with a prescribed exterior sheet and p-divisible disk degrees}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents the following claims relevant to this question, with manuscript numbers following paper order in Sources. In manuscript 1 (family 019; 2026-09-24), the asserted result is that prescribed disjoint small disks on a proper hyperbolic $p$-adic curve admit one connected finite \'{e}tale cover with a sheet over their entire exterior and degree divisible by $p$ on every disk component.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
For manuscript 1 (family 019; 2026-09-24), resolution covers first create positive-genus skeletal vertices, and auxiliary torsors force a cycle over each disk. Degree-$p$ graph characters split over the exterior; a quotient by an exterior stabilizer keeps one exterior sheet while retaining the required disk degrees.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The result supplies the conclusion in this problem with its displayed hypotheses and quantifiers. The broader statements and applications in the manuscript are kept separate from the particular question above. The supporting result is manuscript 1 (family 019; 2026-09-24).

